pokeplatinum-widepointers6.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it after widepointers5): the menus whose entries are
functions (wa2's list, wa3's edits). A StringList entry's index holds the entry's callback in the bag's item actions, the
party menu's context menu, the capsule menu, the underground menus, Mystery Gift and the Wonder Cards: on win64 the exe's
functions are above 4 GB and the u32 index kept the low half only (Linux's exe sits low, so only Windows called the cut
address). The index, StringList_AddFromMessageBank/AddFromString's index, Menu_ProcessInput*'s and ListMenu_ProcessInput's
results, PartyMenu_GetAction, BagApplication_GetItemActionFunc and ItemUseFunction_Get are uintptr_t, and so are the locals
those sites cast to a function pointer. The menus' sentinels come as an int (MENU_CANCEL) or a u32 (0xfffffffe): the
string list stores both sign-extended (WideIndex), and three direct switches on a menu's result use MENU_CANCEL for
their 0xfffffffe label. Also: two weather particles (ov5_021D5EB8.c) keep pointers in their work arrays (intptr_t now),
healthbox.c's VRAM_TRANSFER_DST adds to a uintptr_t, ov61's `long unk_00` is s32 (long is 32-bit on win64, 64 on Linux).
Not changed: battle_anim_system.c's JumpIfEqual/JumpIfUnk_01 (an absolute-address read of a relative word: no script uses them).

